297cc984e872e958456a350f0" :answer-field/choices ["q-339645/field-6/c4b2fef88ba97e017ab533732894399e1b8d9a2297cc984e872e958456a350f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339645" :question/id #uuid "e4c2c806-bfaf-5cf1-a069-1ffb1331bf9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-339645" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-2t\\,{x}_{1}(t)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+5{x}_{1}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n| ${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,x(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |  | {{field-6}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nSuch a system can always be written in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a(t) & b(t) \\\\ c(t) & d(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ g(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have the following system.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-2t\\,{x}_{1}(t)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+5{x}_{1}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2t\\,{x}_{1}(t)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,{x}_{2}(t)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-5{x}_{1}(t)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can rewrite our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2t & 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339645/field-1" "q-339645/field-2" "q-339645/field-3" "q-339645/field-4" "q-339645/field-5" "q-339645/field-6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6dfdbdba-247c-5ddd-bb6e-5d9637140264"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339645"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339372/selection/bea5f482929425f5d642feeb8ad10b577d337f8bcda22cf3f403750becb30447" :answer/id #uuid "130eb812-2442-53a1-b82a-6a4fb3521f3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339372/selection/9b87fd7dfb903b3dc8acae0928d5d897d87f927597da64677da2dd5b2ac7ecd5" :answer/id #uuid "571e29bc-6365-59cb-a712-8e760be49fa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339372/selection/b90a0897f1406bd99f742e8e4b96fb1edc8291c8ce7986e26ec13ab711095755" :answer/id #uuid "96e6d039-387e-51ff-98e3-8dc95a196cf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339372/selection/a4ef175696d8ac6e2253489a23eaab7bc10145d0fa72af9bcad7ddd495c674f0" :answer/id #uuid "2b1ffcfe-f99c-5d9d-ab05-1a60afa51f78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339372/selection/014b7a3ec5a72069802aa9647a0c3b759ba390a91cdb2f14059bb82191f86d05" :answer/id #uuid "895459b6-9b29-5222-84f2-a41e0dd8f640" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339372/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2670ea86-b7ad-5b30-bfdd-6ff59ea36087" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339372/selection/bea5f482929425f5d642feeb8ad10b577d337f8bcda22cf3f403750becb30447" :answer-field/choices ["q-339372/selection/bea5f482929425f5d642feeb8ad10b577d337f8bcda22cf3f403750becb30447" "q-339372/selection/9b87fd7dfb903b3dc8acae0928d5d897d87f927597da64677da2dd5b2ac7ecd5" "q-339372/selection/b90a0897f1406bd99f742e8e4b96fb1edc8291c8ce7986e26ec13ab711095755" "q-339372/selection/a4ef175696d8ac6e2253489a23eaab7bc10145d0fa72af9bcad7ddd495c674f0" "q-339372/selection/014b7a3ec5a72069802aa9647a0c3b759ba390a91cdb2f14059bb82191f86d05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339372" :question/id #uuid "af37968e-c71b-5339-a737-eeb8f1fda04b" :question/math-academy-id "q-339372" :question/problem "If the following system of differential equations is written in the form ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then what is the matrix $A?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+5{x}_{1}(t)-9{x}_{2}(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nSuch a system can always be written in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a(t) & b(t) \\\\ c(t) & d(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ g(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have the following system.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+5{x}_{1}(t)-9{x}_{2}(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-5{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can rewrite our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 9\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339372/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6dfdbdba-247c-5ddd-bb6e-5d9637140264"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339372"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339369/selection/ae43bfcd1736f01b4106f49ebf963a1d0529f536492798c93581cf9166722e2d" :answer/id #uuid "c5936ffa-924f-5fad-94ed-11a4f798e5d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339369/selection/104d29e98f17aa1637b47df6e9b568046519c584f382b0aed022dbaf714fe866" :answer/id #uuid "22c6592e-4966-56d6-ab38-b37bfe63824f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339369/selection/448c743dc5743846e13b7b759bbe9968ad59fa4c47203fd6ea6a451bd45602fd" :answer/id #uuid "2c0a461a-e5b6-5426-a4c2-d8aeb80e9d03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339369/selection/70b44ee36ca82180a562a432d8cab760d9c3d5ac0daeef66f62de7c3ce2ed1c6" :answer/id #uuid "ea3efa34-7715-5049-a9f1-405b1d4757b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} 