\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a(t) & b(t) \\\\ c(t) & d(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ g(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have the following system.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)+3{x}_{1}(t)-5{x}_{2}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)-{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-5{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can rewrite our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339369/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6dfdbdba-247c-5ddd-bb6e-5d9637140264"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339369"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339663/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "d41b6e0c-7086-5917-a6a1-93aebac40c85" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339663/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "69a14d37-7dd6-56cb-bdb8-621990c20473" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339663/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "6a62a466-0a4f-59ba-9045-259e2310fccf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339663/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "8d54f8a6-0ee3-5c08-a630-ed1335ebec81" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339663/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "6c5dbe7b-0943-5110-8f5d-f523ba27b89a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339663/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c67fdfa8-053c-53b5-a0c3-6f57add7c228" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339663/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-339663/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-339663/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-339663/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-339663/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-339663/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339663" :question/id #uuid "754a4a00-918b-5836-9ca9-9c07c3873c1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-339663" :question/problem "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+t\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of the form\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f≡0$ and $g≡0$ (i.e., both $f$ and $g$ are zero functions), then the system is *homogeneous*. Otherwise, if at least one of $f$ or $g$ is not identically zero, the system is *inhomogeneous*.\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is homogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≡0$ and $g≡0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=-2, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=4, &  & d(t)=-1, &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System II is inhomogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $g≢0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=1, &  & b(t)=2, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=-1, &  & d(t)=0, &  & g(t)=t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System III is homogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≡0$ and $g≡0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=0, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=-1, &  & d(t)=0, &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339663/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28939f65-9fd6-564d-a0c2-73c1038ac898"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339663"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339658/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "51a9627b-e217-5d5e-a4cb-7cd0a4be5df9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339658/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "db15d0c5-c9a2-5c35-98bd-4e0513ef3a4c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339658/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "a909c06c-3a76-5768-b967-087ba7ece2f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339658/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "a77b0c29-1f31-50cb-8311-695b299ce18b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339658/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "080ce05f-eb4c-557b-8296-052a87ce66a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339658/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc7d6461-8423-5d1e-acec-3f8c0f024d77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339658/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-339658/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-339658/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-339658/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-339658/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-339658/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339658" :question/id #uuid "042b9e5d-b5c3-529a-afda-b9159a86ab1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-339658" :question/problem "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n\n- ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n- ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n- ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t)$" :question/worked-solution "In matrix form, the system\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=A(t)x(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nis *homogeneous* when $f≡0,$ and *inhomogeneous* when $f≢0.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is homogeneous since $f≡0.$\n\n- System II is homogeneous since $f≡0.$\n\n- System III is homogeneous since $f≡0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339658/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28939f65-9fd6-564d-a0c2-73c1038ac898"] :knowledge-poin